---
import Architecture from '../../layouts/Architecture.astro';
import Diagram from '../../components/arch/Diagram.astro';
import Box from '../../components/arch/Box.astro';
import Edge from '../../components/arch/Edge.astro';
import Group from '../../components/arch/Group.astro';
import Label from '../../components/arch/Label.astro';
import Legend from '../../components/arch/Legend.astro';
---
<Architecture
  title="Overview"
  subtitle="Every moving piece of pixi-reels on one page, and how they are wired."
  eyebrow="Start here"
>
  <p>
    pixi-reels is three rings. The <strong>builder</strong> validates your
    configuration and constructs everything in one <code>build()</code> call.
    The <strong>reel set</strong> is the PixiJS container you add to the stage:
    it owns the reels, the spin controller, the speed profiles and the win
    spotlight. Around that sit two optional subpaths, <strong>testing</strong>
    and <strong>debug</strong>, which never ship in a production bundle unless
    you import them.
  </p>

  <Diagram height={430} caption="What you construct, and what build() hands back. The ReelSet owns six subsystems and one display child, the viewport.">
    <Box x={20} y={20} w={200} h={60} title="Your game" kind="ghost" sub="spin(), setResult(), events" mono={false} />
    <Box x={20} y={120} w={200} h={78} title="ReelSetBuilder" kind="primary" sub={['.reels(5).visibleCells(3)', '.symbols(...).build()']} />
    <Box x={20} y={240} w={200} h={60} title="PIXI.Ticker" kind="code" sub="app.ticker, via TickerRef" />
    <Box x={20} y={330} w={200} h={60} title="gsap" kind="code" sub="per set, via .gsap(instance)" />

    <Edge from={[120, 80]} to={[120, 120]} />
    <Edge from={[220, 159]} to={[260, 159]} label="build()" kind="primary" labelDy={-52} />
    <Edge from={[220, 270]} to={[260, 270]} />
    <Edge from={[220, 360]} to={[260, 360]} />

    <Group x={260} y={20} w={440} h={390} kind="tint" label="ReelSet" note="a PIXI.Container" />
    <Box x={276} y={60} w={200} h={78} title="SpinController" kind="accent" sub={['runs the phases', 'per reel']} />
    <Box x={488} y={60} w={196} h={78} title="SpeedManager" sub={['normal, turbo,', 'super turbo']} />
    <Box x={276} y={154} w={200} h={78} title="FrameBuilder" sub={['which symbols', 'land where']} />
    <Box x={488} y={154} w={196} h={78} title="SymbolFactory" sub={['one ObjectPool', 'per symbol id']} />
    <Box x={276} y={248} w={200} h={78} title="SymbolSpotlight" sub={['dim losers,', 'promote winners']} />
    <Box x={488} y={248} w={196} h={78} title="EventEmitter" sub={['59 typed events', 'spin:*, skip:*, ...']} />
    <Box x={276} y={342} w={408} h={52} title="ReelViewport" kind="subtle" sub="the only display child: five reels under one mask" />
  </Diagram>

  <Diagram height={330} caption="Inside the viewport. Each Reel is a strip longer than the window; the mask hides the buffer cells above and below it.">
    <Group x={20} y={20} w={680} h={290} kind="dashed" label="ReelViewport" note="maskedContainer" />
    {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4].map((i) => (
      <Box
        x={40 + i * 130}
        y={62}
        w={120}
        h={150}
        title={`Reel ${i}`}
        kind="code"
        sub={['ReelAxis', 'ReelMotion', 'StopSequencer', 'ReelSymbol[]']}
      />
    ))}
    <rect x={30} y={100} width={660} height={74} rx="10" class="guide-strong" style="stroke-dasharray: 6 4" />
    <Label x={360} y={244} text="dashed = the visible window (the mask)" anchor="middle" tone="fg" />
    <Label x={360} y={268} text="the symbols above and below it are buffer cells, drawn but clipped" anchor="middle" />
  </Diagram>

  <Diagram height={300} caption="Two subpaths attach from outside and never ship unless imported. Testing swaps the ticker and the art; debug only reads.">
    <Box x={250} y={110} w={220} h={78} title="ReelSet" kind="primary" sub={['the thing on', 'your stage']} />
    <Group x={20} y={20} w={190} h={260} kind="solid" label="pixi-reels/testing" />
    <Box x={34} y={60} w={162} h={52} title="FakeTicker" sub="tick(ms) by hand" />
    <Box x={34} y={126} w={162} h={52} title="HeadlessSymbol" sub="draws nothing" />
    <Box x={34} y={192} w={162} h={66} title="createTestReelSet" size={13} sub={['spinAndLand,', 'expectGrid']} />
    <Group x={510} y={20} w={190} h={260} kind="solid" label="pixi-reels/debug" />
    <Box x={524} y={60} w={162} h={52} title="debugOverlay" sub="12 drawn layers" />
    <Box x={524} y={126} w={162} h={52} title="SpinMetrics" sub="rounds and phases" />
    <Box x={524} y={192} w={162} h={66} title="enableDebug" sub={['main entry:', 'JSON snapshots']} />
    <Edge from={[210, 149]} to={[250, 149]} style="dashed" />
    <Edge from={[510, 149]} to={[470, 149]} style="dashed" />
  </Diagram>

  <div class="not-prose my-8">
    <Legend items={[
      { kind: 'primary', label: 'Entry point', note: 'the one class you construct yourself' },
      { kind: 'accent', label: 'Conductor', note: 'SpinController drives every reel' },
      { kind: 'subtle', label: 'Subsystems', note: 'owned by the ReelSet, destroyed with it' },
      { kind: 'muted', label: 'Optional subpaths', note: 'testing and debug attach from outside' },
    ]} />
  </div>

  <h2>Reading the diagram</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>You construct exactly one class.</strong> <code>ReelSetBuilder</code> is the only <code>new</code> in a typical game. Its <code>build()</code> validates every setting, then constructs the viewport, the symbol pool, the frame pipeline, the reels, and finally the <code>ReelSet</code> that owns them. The <a href="/architecture/builder/">builder page</a> walks that call line by line.</li>
    <li><strong>The ReelSet is a PixiJS container.</strong> <code>app.stage.addChild(reelSet)</code> and it renders. Its only display child is the <code>ReelViewport</code>, which holds the five reel containers under one mask plus the layers above the mask that win presentation uses. See <a href="/architecture/viewport-and-masks/">viewport and masks</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Each reel is a strip, not a column.</strong> A <code>Reel</code> owns an array of symbols longer than the window (buffer cells on both ends), a <code>ReelMotion</code> that derives every symbol's position from its array index, and a <code>StopSequencer</code> that hands out the landing symbols one wrap at a time. See <a href="/architecture/motion/">motion</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>The SpinController only does timing.</strong> It runs each reel through <code>start → spin → [anticipation] → stop</code>, gates stopping on <code>setResult()</code>, and turns button presses into slams or quickens. It draws nothing and decides no outcome. See <a href="/architecture/spin-lifecycle/">spin lifecycle</a> and <a href="/architecture/timeline/">a spin in milliseconds</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Everything talks through typed events.</strong> Two buses: <code>reelSet.events</code> (59 set-level events) and <code>reel.events</code> (7 per-reel events). The full map is on the <a href="/architecture/events/">events page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Testing swaps two things.</strong> A <code>FakeTicker</code> for the Pixi ticker and <code>HeadlessSymbol</code> for the art. Nothing else changes, which is why a full spin runs in Node in milliseconds. See <a href="/architecture/testing/">testing model</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What lives where</h2>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-4">
      <div class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-1">packages/pixi-reels/src/</div>
      <ul class="text-sm space-y-1 text-foreground/80">
        <li><code>core/</code> ReelSet, ReelSetBuilder, Reel, ReelViewport, ReelMotion, ReelAxis, ReelDrive, ReelCurve, ReelWarp, StopSequencer, maskStrategies</li>
        <li><code>spin/</code> SpinController, phases (Start, Spin, Anticipation, Stop, Adjust, Cascade*), steps, modes</li>
        <li><code>symbols/</code> ReelSymbol and the Sprite, AnimatedSprite, Spine, Card, Empty subclasses; SymbolRegistry, SymbolFactory</li>
        <li><code>frame/</code> FrameBuilder, ColumnTarget, RandomSymbolProvider, SymbolPool</li>
        <li><code>config/</code> types, defaults, SpeedPresets, phaseProfile</li>
        <li><code>speed/</code> SpeedManager · <code>spotlight/</code> SymbolSpotlight · <code>wins/</code> WinPresenter</li>
        <li><code>cascade/</code> tumbleAlgorithm, TumbleConfig · <code>board/</code> BoardGrid, Hold &amp; Win · <code>pins/</code> CellPin</li>
        <li><code>events/</code> EventEmitter, ReelEvents · <code>utils/</code> Disposable, TickerRef, gsap, notify</li>
        <li><code>debug/</code> enableDebug (main) and the <code>pixi-reels/debug</code> subpath · <code>testing/</code> the <code>pixi-reels/testing</code> subpath</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-4">
      <div class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-1">apps/site/src/runtime/</div>
      <ul class="text-sm space-y-1 text-foreground/80">
        <li><code>BlurSpriteSymbol.ts</code> sprite symbol with a motion-blur texture swap</li>
        <li><code>CoinSymbol.ts</code> Graphics-drawn coin symbol for Hold &amp; Win</li>
        <li><code>holdAndWinFx.ts</code> coin waves and bezier collect flights</li>
        <li><code>prototypeSpriteLoader.ts</code> the prototype-symbols atlas loader</li>
        <li><code>spineSets.ts</code> the bundled Spine sets behind one interface</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mt-4 mb-1">packages/cheats/src/</div>
      <ul class="text-sm space-y-1 text-foreground/80">
        <li><code>cheats.ts</code> CheatEngine and the built-in forced results</li>
        <li><code>seededRng.ts</code> Mulberry32 PRNG · <code>ways.ts</code> countWays, evaluateWays</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Neither the recipe runtime nor the cheats package is library API. They are
    reference code you copy into your game, which is why they live outside
    <code>packages/pixi-reels/</code> (ADR 009).
  </p>

  <h2>Dependency direction</h2>

  <Diagram height={470} caption="Imports only point downward. No cycles, which is what keeps the testing subpath tree-shakeable.">
    {[
      ['config, events, utils', 'types, DEFAULTS, EventEmitter, TickerRef, gsap'],
      ['pool, symbols, frame', 'ObjectPool, ReelSymbol, FrameBuilder'],
      ['core, per reel', 'Reel, ReelMotion, ReelAxis, ReelViewport'],
      ['spin', 'phases, modes, SpinController'],
      ['core, the set', 'ReelSet, ReelSetBuilder'],
      ['spotlight, wins, board', 'presentation on top of the set'],
    ].map(([t, sub], i) => (
      <Box x={160} y={20 + i * 74} w={400} h={56} title={t} sub={sub} mono={false} kind={i === 4 ? 'primary' : 'subtle'} />
    ))}
    {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4].map((i) => (
      <Edge from={[360, 76 + i * 74]} to={[360, 94 + i * 74]} />
    ))}
  </Diagram>

  <p>
    Read on in order for the full tour, or jump to the page that answers your
    question. Every page has one hand-laid-out diagram per idea and cites the
    file it describes.
  </p>
</Architecture>
